Patch description: add a `target_os = "seraph"` arm to the platform
`cfg_select!` of `library/std/src/sys/alloc/mod.rs`.

Rather than a unified diff (fragile across toolchain bumps), the overlay
code in `xtask/src/rust_src.rs` (`apply_alloc_overlay`) applies this
change by string surgery on the toolchain mirror under `target/`:

 1. Copy `ruststd/src/sys/alloc/seraph.rs` into the mirror at
    `library/std/src/sys/alloc/seraph.rs`.
 2. Read the mirror's `library/std/src/sys/alloc/mod.rs`. If the marker
    `seraph-overlay` is already present, skip.
 3. Otherwise insert the seraph arm immediately after the `zkvm` arm.

The arm selects `seraph.rs` as the platform module `imp`, whose `alloc`,
`alloc_zeroed`, `dealloc`, and `realloc` back both std's `System` allocator
and std's default global allocator (the `__rdl_*` symbols the `alloc` crate
calls when no `#[global_allocator]` is set).
The upstream rust-src is never modified; the mirror is rebuilt whenever
the toolchain or the overlay changes.

The snippet inserted:

    // seraph-overlay: seraph alloc (pub(crate) so os::seraph can reach it)
    target_os = "seraph" => {
        pub(crate) mod seraph;
        use seraph as imp;
    }
